Link NSS's SPARC freebl implementation into libxul.

Related Mozilla import:
  imports/solaris-freebl3-os-libs.patch
  Petr Sumbera, "SPARC: use Solaris freebl library for nss-rs links",
  Tue Jun 23 2026.

NSS does not build freebl3 on this platform.  It builds freebl_64fpu_3, which
exports the FREEBL_GetVector entry point required by nss-rs.

The earlier import selected freebl_64fpu_3 in the nss-rs build script. Firefox
153 validates and links its non-system NSS library through
toolkit/library/moz.build, so select the same implementation at that layer.

--- firefox-153.0/toolkit/library/moz.build
+++ firefox-153.0/toolkit/library/moz.build
@@ -165,8 +165,10 @@
 # For system NSS, freebl is linked by the nss-rs build.rs via pkg-config instead.
 if not CONFIG["MOZ_SYSTEM_NSS"]:
     if CONFIG["OS_TARGET"] == "Linux":
         USE_LIBS += ["freeblpriv3"]
+    elif CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "SunOS" and CONFIG["TARGET_CPU"] == "sparc64":
+        USE_LIBS += ["freebl_64fpu_3"]
     else:
         USE_LIBS += ["freebl3"]
 
 if not CONFIG["USE_LIBZ_RS"]:
